# Code owners for the agentic security benchmark.
#
# Every path is owned, so every pull request requires review. This is deliberate: the corpora and
# the scoring rules are the entire product here, and a benchmark whose samples or scoring can
# change without review is not a benchmark anyone should cite.
#
# Enable "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch protection rules for this to be enforced
# rather than advisory.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                       @gitayg

# The corpora. Adding, removing or relabelling a sample changes numbers already published for
# every product scored on this benchmark, including other vendors' submitted results.
/corpora/               @gitayg

# The scoring harness and adapters. A change here silently re-prices every published result.
/scorers/               @gitayg

# Published results. Never merged across products; each product's numbers stay on its own lines.
/results/               @gitayg

# Contribution workflow, issue forms, PR template and CI. The validator in test/ is the gate that
# keeps locked splits and credential-shaped strings out of the tree.
/.github/               @gitayg
/test/                  @gitayg

# Top-level documentation: the methodology, the AMTSO mapping, and the contribution rules are
# load-bearing claims, not prose.
/*.md                   @gitayg
/CODEOWNERS             @gitayg
/LICENSE                @gitayg
/NOTICE                 @gitayg
/package.json           @gitayg
